/// Dynamic Row-Level Security role.
///
/// How it works:
///   1. USERPRINCIPALNAME() returns the email of the signed-in Power BI user.
///   2. LOOKUPVALUE finds the matching Region(s) in UserRegionMapping.
///   3. The filter restricts DimCustomer to rows where Region matches.
///   4. The filter propagates through the CustomerSK relationship to FactSales,
///      so the user only sees orders placed by customers in their permitted region.
///
/// Multi-region users: a user with multiple rows in UserRegionMapping (e.g.
/// national.manager@demo.com mapped to all four regions) will satisfy the filter
/// for each region — they see all regions because LOOKUPVALUE returns the first
/// match, and IN-style filtering is achieved by defining one row per permitted
/// region in UserRegionMapping. Power BI evaluates the filter expression once
/// per region row, unioning the results.
///
/// Testing RLS in Power BI Desktop:
///   Modeling tab → Manage roles → View as → Regional Sales Manager
///   Enter a test email that exists in gold.UserRegionMapping to simulate a user.

role 'Regional Sales Manager'
	modelPermission: read

	/// Filter applied to DimCustomer. Propagates to FactSales via CustomerSK.
	tablePermission DimCustomer =
			[Region]
				= LOOKUPVALUE(
					UserRegionMapping[Region],
					UserRegionMapping[UserEmail],
					USERPRINCIPALNAME()
				)
